[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479823072","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2479823072","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99297","id":2479823072,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Tzxjg","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T19:57:56Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T19:57:56Z","body":"To illustrate the issue, this is the signature of the related `_parse_file` method, which is being fixed in the related PR:\r\n```cpp\r\n        virtual void _parse_file(const String &p_path, const TypedArray<String> &p_msgids, const TypedArray<Array> &p_msgids_context_plural);\r\n```\r\nHaven't generated the headers for the current state but `_get_comments` will have the same signature and you need to `const_cast` those arguments, which is very unintuitive and fragile","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2479823072/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2485028786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2485028786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99297","id":2485028786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UHoey","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-19T08:33:11Z","updated_at":"2024-11-19T08:34:59Z","body":"I'm not familiar with the GDExtension issue, but it looks good to me as long as `_get_comments()` is consistent with `_parse_file()` (so I would prefer #92175 to be merged or at least approved first). However, I have a question:\r\n\r\n1. If we decide to break `_parse_file()` compatibility, maybe it makes sense to combine `_parse_file()` and `_get_comments()` into a single method that returns a table (`Array[PackedStringArray]`, `Array[Array]`, or `Array[Dictionary]`) with the columns `msgid`, `msgctxt`, `msgid_plural`, and `comment`? The required column would be `msgid`, the others can be left blank. I don't think it makes sense to separate `msgids` and `msgids_context_plural` as it is now, because it's all a single table under the hood anyway.\r\n2. If we want to maintain maximum compatibility, we could add a `_parse_file_ext()` or `_parse_file_2()` method and deprecate `_parse_file()`. This is more related to #92175, as `_get_comments()` did not appear in any stable release.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2485028786/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2486147089","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2486147089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99297","id":2486147089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UL5gR","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-19T16:12:07Z","updated_at":"2024-11-19T16:18:10Z","body":"That makes sense, will test some alternatives for deprecation and update as needed\r\n\r\nI'm not familiar enough with the code here to say if merging the two methods into one is feasible, but if it is might merging the two, dropping `_get_comments` and deprecating `_parse_file`, work?\r\n\r\nThe new method could be `_parse_file_and_comments` or something, would be less obscure to have as a replacement maybe\r\n\r\nThat way we could possibly detect if `_parse_file_and_comments` or what we call it is bound, and otherwise call the outdated one\r\n\r\nWould depend on if we consider deprecation worth it, unsure what happens in other languages but it is possible to use it in godot-cpp but requires casting, I don't know how it works in C# though so confirming how the current methods work or don't work for plugins made in C# would be good\r\n\r\nIt does seem that these cases *do* work with plugins in GDScript so that's a reason to deprecate over entirely replacing, but will test with GDScript soon to confirm","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2486147089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487899084","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2487899084","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99297","id":2487899084,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6USlPM","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T08:39:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T08:39:51Z","body":"> I don't know how it works in C# though so confirming how the current methods work or don't work for plugins made in C# would be good\r\n\r\nI haven't tested personally but since Arrays in C# are reference types I imagine they may work. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99195 uses the method so, assuming the PR works, it would prove that the method works in C#.\r\n\r\nAlso, how is the GDExtension validation not complaining about breaking compatibility? Does it not check virtual methods?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487899084/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487912246","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2487912246","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99297","id":2487912246,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6USoc2","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T08:45:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T08:45:40Z","body":"> Also, how is the GDExtension validation not complaining about breaking compatibility? Does it not check virtual methods?\r\n\r\n`EditorTranslationParserPlugin._get_comments()` is not in 4.3 stable. Only #92175 breaks compatibility, this PR can be considered as a non-breaking part of #92175.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487912246/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487940816","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2487940816","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99297","id":2487940816,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6USvbQ","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-20T08:58:27Z","updated_at":"2024-11-20T08:58:27Z","body":"> I'm not familiar enough with the code here to say if merging the two methods into one is feasible, but if it is might merging the two, dropping `_get_comments` and deprecating `_parse_file`, work?\r\n> \r\n> The new method could be `_parse_file_and_comments` or something, would be less obscure to have as a replacement maybe\r\n> \r\n> That way we could possibly detect if `_parse_file_and_comments` or what we call it is bound, and otherwise call the outdated one\r\n\r\nI guess it depends on how we handle other cases in #92175. Yes, the fact that it seems to work in GDScript and C# is an argument for deprecation instead of removal/replacement. However, I don't think `EditorTranslationParserPlugin` is used very often, so breaking compatibility there is more acceptable than with core APIs like `Object`, `Node`, etc.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2487940816/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2488010621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99297#issuecomment-2488010621","issue_url":"https://